---
description: Require a squash-commit changelog line as its own commit on every PR
alwaysApply: true
---

# Changelog entries

Every pull request must add **one** line to `CHANGELOG.md` under `## [Unreleased]`.

The line is exactly the squash-merge subject and the PR number. The squash subject is the PR title (Conventional Commits). Do not invent a different summary.

```markdown
- <pr title> (#<pr number>)
```

```
# ❌ BAD
- Improved linting
- feat(proto): add lot spec
  (missing PR number; mixed into the feature commit)

# ✅ GOOD
- feat(proto): add lot spec (#12)
  (own commit that only changes CHANGELOG.md)
```

## Separate commit

The changelog line is **always** its own commit:

- That commit touches **only** `CHANGELOG.md`
- Do not mix the line with schema, CI, docs, or other edits
- Open the PR first, then add this commit once the number is known
- If the PR title changes, update the line to match

Do not commit the changelog line until the PR exists. Feature commits land first; the changelog commit is last.
